/-!
# Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] at the source's own hypotheses

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme, `𝓘 ⊂ 𝒪_X` an **arbitrary** quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals
and `K` an **arbitrary** object of `D(𝒪_X)`. Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] asserts

`K^∧ = R lim (K ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_X} 𝒪_X/𝓘ⁿ)`.

This file proves it, with `K^∧` the derived completion of [Stacks, Tag 099F] along `𝓘` and
`R lim` read, as everywhere in the library, as the predicate
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit`. Nothing beyond the source's hypotheses is asked:
no quasi-compactness of `X`, no generation of `𝓘` by global sections, nothing of `K`. The earlier
registration `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_derivedTensor_adicQuotientSystem_completion`
of `Completion/KoszulAdicDerivedTensorLimit.lean` needed both of the first two.

## The proof

The source's proof says "we may work locally". That is not a formality: `R lim` names no map, and
two objects that are derived limits of the same tower on every member of a cover need not be
derived limits of it globally. What makes the step legitimate is a comparison map given by a
formula. For a K-flat representative `K̃` of `K`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj` is a named derived limit `L` of the tower,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.kInjectiveAdicComparison` a named map `K ⟶ L`, and the map
`K^∧ ⟶ L` the universal property of the derived completion attaches to it
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pinnedAdicComparison`) restricts over each open `U` to the slice's
own pinned comparison ([Stacks, Tag 0A0F]); being an isomorphism is local, which is the
chart-wise reduction `isDerivedLimit_derivedCompletion_adicReductionTower_of_coversTop_slice`.

On an affine open `U` the ideal is generated by finitely many sections over `U`
(`Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal_affine`), the Koszul cohomology
sheaves are pro-zero below the top degree there ([Stacks, Tag 0921] at the single model
`Γ(U, 𝒪)`, `Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_koszulDualSystemOn_over_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_section`),
the restriction of `L` is a derived limit of the slice's own tower with the restriction of the
named map as its derived reductions
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_isDerivedLimitWithProjections_map_kInjectiveAdicMilnorObj`),
and the slice's pinned comparison is then an isomorphism by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_pinnedAdicComparison_of_exists_factor`: matching the
projections of two presentations does not make a comparison invertible in general, but after each
`R𝑆heafHom(K^k, -)` the tower factors eventually through a constant
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_factor_derivedSheafHomSystem_koszulPowerSystem`, the
Koszul-index input, from the null-homotopy of [Stacks, Tag 0663]), which removes the phantom
indeterminacy of [Stacks, Tag 0919], and those functors detect isomorphisms between
derived-complete objects ([Stacks, Tag 0A0E]).

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_derivedCompletion` — **part (1) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]**.

